            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 84-year-old male patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he exhibited significant dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. The patient was promptly commenced on supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Continuous pulse oximetry was maintained throughout the stay. Clinical response was satisfactory, with gradual improvement in respiratory function. The patient was discharged in a stable condition. I recommend continuation of his inhaled bronchodilator therapy and close monitoring in your practice. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
